# MQL5 LBS ATR Scheduled Stop Breakout

## Source
- Source: [[sources/mql5-codebase-mt5-strategies]]
- Page / Timestamp: MQL5 CodeBase, "LBS - expert for MetaTrader 5", idea by Scriptor, code by Vladimir Karputov / barabashkakvn, published 2018-12-28, updated 2019-01-17, https://www.mql5.com/en/code/22884

## Mechanics

### Entry
- Baseline symbols: liquid DWX FX majors, XAUUSD.DWX, oil, and liquid index CFDs.
- Timeframe: M15 or H1; baseline H1 for lower noise.
- At each new bar, allow setup only when current hour equals one of three configured source hours.
- Compute ATR(14) on bar #0.
- Define recent maximum and minimum from bars #0 and #1.
- Place Buy Stop at max(bar #0, bar #1) + ATR(14).
- Place Sell Stop at min(bar #0, bar #1) - ATR(14).
- When one pending order is filled, cancel all remaining sibling pending orders.

### Exit
- Baseline TP = 2R.
- Time stop: close open position after 12 H1 bars or at end of trading day, whichever comes first.
- Cancel unfilled pending orders at the next configured setup hour or at day end.

### Stop Loss
- V5 baseline: SL = ATR(14) from entry, fixed at order placement.
- Source says trailing is applied; V5 baseline disables trailing for first build and can test fixed-step trailing as a later parameter variant.

### Position Sizing
- V5 baseline: fixed-risk $1,000 per backtest trade.
- Source supports fixed lot or risk percent; V5 uses standard fixed-risk backtest conventions.

### Additional filters
- One-position-per-magic.
- Do not place new orders if spread exceeds V5 default threshold.
- No simultaneous opposing positions after fill; sibling pending orders are cancelled.
- No grid, martingale, averaging, or adaptive sizing.

